    <!-- Monterrey Descriptions -->
    <string name="mty_fundidora_desc">Inclusive urban park, bastion of industrial history with green areas, museums, and cultural walk.</string>
    <string name="mty_santa_lucia_desc">A 2.5 km navigable canal considered one of the 13 man-made wonders of Mexico.</string>
    <string name="mty_macroplaza_desc">One of the largest public squares in the world, the cultural and historic heart of the city.</string>
    <string name="mty_cerro_silla_desc">The most important natural icon and characteristic symbol of the city of Monterrey.</string>
    <string name="mty_barrio_antiguo_desc">Historic area with 19th-century architecture, art galleries, coffee shops, dining, and nightlife.</string>
    <string name="mty_marco_desc">Contemporary Art Museum of Monterrey, internationally recognized for its exhibitions.</string>
    <string name="mty_obispado_desc">Summit of Obispado Hill featuring a spectacular panoramic view and the Monumental Flag.</string>
    <string name="mty_chipinque_desc">Natural reserve in the Sierra Madre Oriental ideal for hiking, cycling, and wildlife watching.</string>
    <string name="mty_bbva_desc">Modern soccer stadium, home of Rayados de Monterrey and venue for the FIFA World Cup.</string>
    <string name="mty_volcan_uanl_desc">Home of Tigres UANL, famous for the passion of its fans and rich sports tradition.</string>
    <string name="mty_grutas_garcia_desc">Millenary underground formations of stalagmites and stalactites in the municipality of García.</string>
    <string name="mty_catedral_desc">Beautiful Novohispanic Baroque cathedral with centuries of history in the heart of Monterrey.</string>
